  branch point at t ~ -2874440312387 .. -2874440580608   (paper's own estimate: ~ -2.8e12)

Conclusion: the alpha=0 specialization IS totally real (28 real roots) for t in roughly (that branch point, 0), matching Theorem 4.2's own claimed interval closely -- confirming the underlying theorem even though the printed Corollary 4.3 coefficients did not reproduce it for us.

